# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the nightly ASan CI job.
#
# `create_annex` is the vendored `v8` crate's own per-isolate bookkeeping
# allocation (IsolateAnnex) — not code owned by this repo, and not
# something we can fix here. It's tiny (8 bytes) and one-time per isolate
# (one per process in a real 3va run, reclaimed by the OS at exit); it only
# shows up as an ASan finding because the test binary creates and drops
# many isolates in one process. Everything in `crates/js` is expected to be
# leak-clean — see `builtins::NativeCtxRegistry` and
# `shared_array_buffer_allocator()` in crates/js/src/lib.rs for how the
# equivalent 'static-native-data problems are actually fixed (not just
# suppressed) on our side.
leak:*Isolate*create_annex*
